11/20/2006&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
I fished today with Jack Libaire and his friend Brian right to left.  We had an interesting day.  We found shad and caught a bunch and a schoolie bass.  We went into the ocean with birds diving but no fish.  We set up for sea duck hunting east of the inlet.  The ducks came pretty good and we had about 10 goes at them.  We knocked down three and bagged two scooters.  A friend of mine called and said he was into bass on the inside.  He had three fish of 30 pounds, 28 pounds and 22 pounds.  When we got there it was all but over.  We found a pod of bunker and I cast netted a bunch.  We then had one bass on but dropped it.  We the had another couple of run offs but no fish.  No bass to eat just ducks and not the best eating kind.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
I really think we are in for another shot of fish.  The water was 59 degrees and bait all over the place.  This season is not over.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Jack and Brian were tough on a cold day with mixed results.  The best part was the sea ducks coming in like chickens to a small decoy rig.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Another good day on the water with good sportsmen.  Always a pleasure.&lt;br /&gt;
&lt;br /&gt;
Captain Al Lorenzetti
